          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A standard radon test takes 2 to 4 days of exposure after 12 hours of closed-house conditions, plus about a week or two for the lab to return the result. Real estate tests run at least 48 hours, long-term tests run 90 days or more, and digital monitors give a first number within a day or two but need weeks to produce an average you should act on.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your first result is 4 pCi/L or higher, follow up and plan to mitigate; between 2 and 4, consider it. Either way, the test is quick and cheap compared with what it protects against. Our <a href="/best-radon-detector/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-semibold hover:underline">best radon detector</a> picks cover the kits and monitors worth buying.
